`lib/WWW/DNSMadeEasy/ManagedDomain.pm`: `records()` now builds the list query with `URI->query_form`, so `recordName` and `type` are percent-encoded. The old code glued them raw onto the path ("?recordName=" . $args{name}).

`t/14-records-query-form.t` only uses "www" and "A". Without special characters the query is identical to the old build, so the test is green against the old lib/ and holds nothing of the escaping. The Changes entry says "no wire change" accordingly - true for the values in the test, but the encoding itself is recorded nowhere.

Done when:

- a case with a name that has to be escaped (a space, `+` or `&`) shows the built query and is red against the old lib/ (behavioural failure, not "cannot locate")
- the Changes entry names the encoding instead of saying "no wire change" (destination, not journey: the name is encoded safely into the query)

The test has to check the built query, not just that nothing happens.

